    ["e041704"] = "Moonfire on the cursor: to put DOTs on several enemies (change to Insect Swarm for the other one).",
    ["11b387e"] = "Feral Charge (cat) and then Prowl, if you are not already stealthed.",
    ["9bca5ec"] = "Changes form to free yourself from roots and slows: from bear to cat, from cat to cat.",
    ["38e0846"] = "One button: Aquatic Form in water, Travel Form outdoors, otherwise Cat Form.",
    ["53406a7"] = "Enters Dire Bear Form once only, without leaving it if you press again.",
    ["b18da61"] = "Growl on the focus, then on the cursor, then on the target.",
    ["beb6029"] = "Nature's Swiftness and right away Healing Touch: an instant emergency heal (leaves the form and stops the cast).",
    ["8c5c182"] = "Macros cannot be created in combat: try again later.",
    ["e3c93a8"] = "Macros: %d created, %d updated%s. Open them with /macro and drag them onto your bars.",
    ["99effc3"] = "%d not created (you already have 18 character macros)",
    ["530c645"] = "There are no macros for this spec.",
    ["1e74c8f"] = "BuildBeast will create %s macros for your character:\n%s\n\nIf they already exist it updates them. Then you drag them onto your bars.",
    ["d8354a3"] = "Create",
    ["160009a"] = "Cancel",
    ["054716f"] = "Warrior",
    ["3e76e85"] = "Paladin",
    ["69c8129"] = "Hunter",
    ["dd6c053"] = "Rogue",
    ["3a3f441"] = "Priest",
    ["fabeb14"] = "Shaman",
    ["a5a0a92"] = "Mage",
    ["8b0635d"] = "Warlock",
    ["3d8e8ed"] = "Druid",
    ["ce774d9"] = "YES",
    ["c2f3f48"] = "NO",
    ["672c529"] = "SIMILAR",
    ["656ff24"] = "Bear Form, Growl, Maul (class quest), Nature's Grasp, Demoralizing Roar",
    ["50d1ea3"] = "Bash; quest for Cure Poison",
    ["2290f2a"] = "Swipe; quest for Aquatic Form",
    ["227f378"] = "Faerie Fire (now also in forms), Hibernate",
    ["469f184"] = "Cat Form (quest), Prowl, Claw, Rip, Shred, Starfire, Rebirth, Omen of Clarity",
    ["eda7053"] = "Mark of the Wild on yourself. Open with Wrath and keep casting it. When mana is low finish the monster with your weapon, so mana comes back. Heal with Healing Touch between fights.",
    ["3d495a9"] = "Keep Mark of the Wild and Thorns on yourself and put Rejuvenation on before engaging. Open with Wrath, add Moonfire and keep casting Wrath. In a crowded area open with Moonfire, which is instant.",
    ["bb21cc8"] = "The class quest gives you Bear Form, Growl and Maul. Nature's Grasp roots the next monster that hits you; Demoralizing Roar is for bear form.",
    ["a9ba21f"] = "Enrage gives you rage at once and more in 10 seconds, but lowers your armor.",
    ["9c7f3ca"] = "Feral is the cat and bear spec, and the one that levels most smoothly: Prowl and Dash take you from one objective to the next and you almost never stop for mana. In Bear Form: Mark of the Wild and Thorns on yourself, and let the rage from your hits pay for Maul, which adds damage to the next hit. Against several monsters Demoralizing Roar to weaken them.",
    ["ce230c2"] = "In Bear Form: Enrage before the pull (the armor loss matters less), Faerie Fire lowers the monster's armor, Swipe is the filler and Maul spends the leftover rage. With several monsters Demoralizing Roar first, then Swipe.",
    ["78a0920"] = "Cat Form: Mark of the Wild and Thorns first. Open from Prowl with Shred (Prowl takes you behind the monster), then Faerie Fire, then Claw to build combo points or Shred when you are behind. With four or more combo points Rip if the monster lives long enough. Bear Form stays better against several monsters: cat form has nothing that hits more than one.",
    ["540175c"] = "Rake: open from Prowl with Shred, Faerie Fire, then Rake and keep its bleed always active on a monster that lives long enough; then Claw or Shred from behind. With 4 or more points: Rip if the monster lives, Ferocious Bite to finish.",
    ["87e3251"] = "Lacerate (bear): a bleed that stacks up to 5 times; against a single monster it is your filler, and Maul spends the leftover rage. With several monsters Demoralizing Roar and then Swipe. Blood Frenzy: in bear every crit gives 5 rage, in cat a crit with a combo point ability gives one more.",
    ["25dc320"] = "Predatory Discipline: Ferocious Bite still gains damage from the extra energy, but does not spend it.",
    ["042c952"] = "Ravage: open from Prowl with Ravage (you must be behind the monster), then Faerie Fire, Rake with the bleed always active, then Claw or Shred from behind; with 4 or more points Rip or Ferocious Bite to finish. Poised removes 10 energy from your first hit if you start at full energy.",
    ["4560b4d"] = "Dire Bear Form: Enrage before the pull, Faerie Fire, Primal Bite at every cooldown (a strong bite with a 6 second cooldown and lots of threat), Lacerate in between against a single monster and Maul to spend the rest; with several monsters Demoralizing Roar and Swipe in place of Lacerate.",
    ["ff10d54"] = "Cat: Shifting Power when you have less than 50 energy (turns mana into 40 energy, 8 second cooldown).",
    ["0d8ecd7"] = "Feral wants above all the weapon's damage per second, because your form is based on it, and weapon speed does not matter. Then Hit, crit, Agility and Strength.",
    ["4a841e3"] = "Guardian is the bear: it uses the same talent plan as Feral. Bear Form with Mark of the Wild and Thorns on yourself; the rage from your hits pays for Maul. Against several monsters Demoralizing Roar.",
    ["7b551a8"] = "Enrage before the pull, Faerie Fire on the monster, Swipe as the filler and Maul with the leftover rage. With several monsters Demoralizing Roar then Swipe.",
    ["af4c8fb"] = "Lacerate is your filler against a single monster (it stacks up to 5 times); Maul spends the leftover rage. With several monsters Demoralizing Roar and Swipe.",
    ["5213241"] = "Dire Bear Form: Enrage before the pull, Faerie Fire, Primal Bite at every cooldown (6 seconds, lots of threat), Lacerate in between against a single monster and Maul for the rest; with several monsters Demoralizing Roar and Swipe in place of Lacerate.",
    ["fc61247"] = "The bear wants the weapon's damage per second (speed does not matter), then Hit, crit, Agility and Strength. For bear form Strength and spell power are fine too, and Stamina matters more if you tank.",
    ["25acd2a"] = "Balance and Restoration start the same: Improved Wrath (half a second less casting time and half the mana) and Nature's Focus. Balance starts slow, but speeds up when Insect Swarm joins Moonfire on every monster.",
    ["9c1fb9f"] = "Mark of the Wild and Thorns on yourself, Rejuvenation before engaging. Open with Wrath, or Moonfire if the area is crowded. Moonfire and Insect Swarm on the monster (a DOT that also lowers its chance to hit), then Wrath. Regrowth if you need healing, Nature's Grasp before a second monster arrives.",
    ["7f51b3b"] = "Moonfire and Insect Swarm on every monster you fight, then Wrath. With three or more monsters, Hurricane.",
    ["c845919"] = "With three or more monsters, Barkskin and then Hurricane.",
    ["d66aa4c"] = "Eclipse: every Wrath takes half a second off your next two Starfires, so Starfire finally enters the rotation: one Wrath followed by two Starfires.",
    ["7e94c11"] = "Moonkin Form: lots of armor, 3% crit for the group and Omen of Clarity triggers twice as often; you cannot cast heals while in it, so leave it for Regrowth and go back in. Rotation: Moonfire and Insect Swarm, then one Wrath and two Starfires.",
    ["ef6797a"] = "For Balance and Restoration spell power comes first, then Intellect, crit and Spirit; Restoration adds healing power at 60. A caster staff can come from a faction quest.",
    ["a91a8ac"] = "Restoration is the slowest to level, because healing does not kill monsters: you can level as Balance or Feral and still heal dungeons.",
    ["7a2110b"] = "Mark of the Wild and Thorns on yourself, Rejuvenation before engaging. Open with Wrath or Moonfire in a crowded area, then Moonfire and Insect Swarm on the monster and Wrath. Regrowth if you need healing, Nature's Grasp before a second monster arrives.",
    ["937f66e"] = "Swiftmend: instant heal on whoever has your Rejuvenation or Regrowth. When you take damage, Swiftmend on your Rejuvenation and then Regrowth if you need more. With three or more monsters, Hurricane.",
    ["2061d06"] = "Nature's Swiftness: your next nature spell is instant. Keep it out of the rotation, for the moment you need a big heal right now.",
    ["1164b95"] = "Wild Growth: heals the target and its group over 7 seconds, stronger at the start: in a group when more than one person is hurt.",
    ["8f8a34a"] = "Aspect of the Hawk, taming the pet (class quest: Tame Beast, Call Pet, Feed Pet, Revive Pet)",
    ["2b3db50"] = "Auto Shot starts by itself: stand still half a second before every shot and let the monster come. Raptor Strike if it reaches you. Within 8 yards ranged shots do not work.",
    ["9329f10"] = "Add Serpent Sting as an opener, only on monsters that last: if it dies in a few seconds the damage is wasted.",
    ["d2b7bf1"] = "Hunter's Mark before the pull, then Serpent Sting. Arcane Shot when you have mana.",
    ["85f72cd"] = "The core is Auto Shot, with Arcane Shot when you have mana. Before the pull Hunter's Mark, then Serpent Sting as the opener. While the monster runs at you Concussive Shot slows it; Raptor Strike if it reaches you.",
    ["71067ff"] = "You have the pet: send it in for a few seconds, then Serpent Sting. Always keep Aspect of the Hawk up and feed the pet. Concussive Shot if the monster turns on you, Raptor Strike as a last resort.",
    ["bb6f64b"] = "Rapid Fire (+40% attack speed for 15 seconds) stays out of the rotation: keep it for the pull that needs it.",
    ["ebe54cf"] = "The core is Aimed Shot every time it is ready (2 second cast, 6 second cooldown shared with Multi-Shot), with Auto Shot in the gaps. Before the pull Hunter's Mark, pet in first, then Serpent Sting. Arcane Shot when you have mana. If the monster reaches you: Disengage. With several monsters: Multi-Shot in place of Aimed Shot.",
    ["c943332"] = "The core is the hawks (Summon Hawk): each hawk lasts 18 seconds, two can be out; summon a new hawk when one of the two expires. Then Aimed Shot when ready and Auto Shot in the gaps. Arcane Shot uses the same cooldown as the hawks, so wait until after them. The rest as before.",
    ["ab9f050"] = "Add Intimidation: if the monster turns on you it stuns and gives threat to the pet; Disengage when it is not ready. With several monsters: Explosive Trap first, then Multi-Shot on the Aimed Shot cooldown.",
    ["bf06335"] = "Bestial Wrath (2 minutes) and Volley stay out of the rotation: use them by hand on dangerous pulls or with big groups. From 42 almost all points go into Marksmanship: the rotation does not change.",
    ["e096af7"] = "Beast Mastery shoots from afar: ranged weapon DPS matters, then Agility. The melee weapon is only for its stats.",
    ["b35c3c9"] = "The core is Aimed Shot every time it is ready, with Auto Shot in the gaps. After the pet's head start the first shot must be the strongest: with Rapid Killing waiting it is Aimed Shot. Before the pull Hunter's Mark and pet in; Serpent Sting on every monster, because if it dies with Serpent Sting on it your next shot within 20 seconds does up to 20% more. Arcane Shot when you have mana. If the monster reaches you: Disengage. With several monsters: Multi-Shot in place of Aimed Shot.",
    ["cf4e14e"] = "Before the pull Trueshot Aura too, besides Hunter's Mark.",
    ["51e16cf"] = "Sniper Shot is your strongest shot: 4 second cast, 15 second cooldown, up to 45 yards, and for 10 seconds your next three shots reach 10 yards further. Use it as the first shot after the pet's head start when you have time for the cast, better with Rapid Killing waiting; otherwise Aimed Shot. With several monsters: Explosive Trap first, then Multi-Shot on the Aimed Shot cooldown.",
    ["c8aaa16"] = "The core is the hawks (Summon Hawk): a new one every time one of the two expires. Then Aimed Shot when ready and Auto Shot in the gaps; Sniper Shot as the first shot if you have time. Arcane Shot waits until after the hawks.",
    ["1fe9ee6"] = "Marksmanship shoots from afar: ranged weapon DPS matters (all else equal, a slower one with big hits is better, because Aimed Shot is based on a weapon hit) and Agility. With Careful Aim Intellect also counts as attack power, besides mana. The melee weapon is only for its stats.",
    ["184fc61"] = "Survival fights in two places. At range: Multi-Shot every time it is ready (it is instant and shares its cooldown with Aimed Shot, so you almost never use Aimed Shot), plus Serpent Sting, Arcane Shot and Auto Shot. In melee: Immolation Trap, then Raptor Strike (instant, 6 second cooldown) and Mongoose Bite after a dodge. Hunter's Mark before the pull and the pet goes in first.",
    ["d85837a"] = "Strider Kick: a kick with the weapon's full damage that makes you 30% faster for 3 seconds: it is the button that ends the melee and takes you back to range. In melee first Immolation Trap, Mongoose Bite when usable, Raptor Strike. At range Multi-Shot when ready, Serpent Sting, Arcane Shot, Auto Shot. With several monsters Explosive Trap takes the place of Immolation Trap, because a single cooldown covers all traps.",
    ["e7233e1"] = "With Lacerating Strikes every Mongoose Bite leaves a bleed equal to 40% of the hit's damage, over 21 seconds.",
    ["10bfe36"] = "Survival shoots but also hits with the melee weapon (Raptor Strike and Strider Kick are based on its damage): a slow two-hander helps. Then Agility matters. From 49 Careful Aim makes Intellect useful as attack power too.",
    ["0718298"] = "Blink, Evocation, Mana Shield, Blizzard, Fire Ward, teleport to two capitals (and Arcane Blast for Arcane and Fire)",
    ["ad986c1"] = "Conjure Mana Agate (the first mana gem)",
    ["3e67dd9"] = "Ice Armor; class quest (the Ice Fury wand)",
    ["3ddbf7c"] = "Frostfire Bolt, first portals",
    ["3d9e7fb"] = "Always keep Arcane Intellect and an armor spell up (for now Frost Armor). Mana regeneration stops for 5 seconds after every spell that costs mana: an almost dead monster is not worth a full cast. Around level 5 get a wand (an Enchanter makes you the Lesser Magic Wand, the Greater Magic Wand from 13): until talents it can do as much damage as your spells or more and it spends no mana.",
    ["2991425"] = "Open with Frostbolt at maximum range, so the monster arrives slowed. Keep casting while it approaches, then Fire Blast to finish and the wand for what is left.",
    ["5d6b9a7"] = "Frost Nova freezes everything around you: damage breaks it, so you can step back and keep casting. If the monster reaches melee: Frost Nova and step back.",
    ["11f2d67"] = "With Missile Barrage: open from afar with Frostbolt (Arcane and Frost) or Fireball (Fire), keep casting and when the proc triggers cast Arcane Missiles: they become a free volley. Missile Barrage is the talent that saves you the most mana while leveling.",
    ["b985201"] = "Evocation is an 8 second channel that gives you back most of your mana. Blink on cooldown while running makes you arrive about a fifth faster. The hearthstone is better used for the quest zone, because the teleport already takes you to a capital.",
    ["a601e53"] = "Arcane Blast: every cast gives you spell damage equal to 12% of your Intellect, up to 4 charges that last 18 seconds; each charge makes the next cast cost 100% more. Frostbolt from afar, then Arcane Blast one to three times until Missile Barrage triggers, then Arcane Missiles. Let the charges expire instead of reaching four. Spend Clear Casting on a charged Arcane Blast. In melee: Frost Nova and step back. Fire Blast to finish and the wand.",
    ["e55eb73"] = "Arcane Wrath: a heavy hit with a 6 second cooldown (the extra damage is worth 5% of your maximum mana). Frostbolt from afar, then Arcane Wrath, Arcane Blast one to three times until Missile Barrage and Arcane Missiles; Frost Nova when it gets close, Arcane Wrath again, then Fire Blast and the wand for the kill. Let the charges expire or the rising cost drains you; Clear Casting only on a charged Arcane Blast or an Arcane Wrath, never on a cheap spell.",
    ["65a5bf0"] = "Presence of Mind: your next spell with a cast under 10 seconds is instant.",
    ["c51b464"] = "Arcane Power: +30% damage for 15 seconds, at the cost of +30% mana.",
    ["dfc4101"] = "Open with Pyroblast or Frostbolt from afar, then Arcane Wrath. Arcane Blast one to three times until Missile Barrage, then the missiles. From 58 Fire Blast on cooldown and Pyroblast when Heating Up reaches 3 charges.",
    ["9226a40"] = "For every spec spell power comes first, because your spells scale a lot with it. Intellect raises mana and a little crit; Spirit reduces the pauses to drink, and for Arcane it matters a lot because it burns mana quickly.",
    ["ebbbb02"] = "Fireball from afar. One or two Arcane Blasts until Missile Barrage triggers, then the missiles. Fire Blast on cooldown. A monster with little health does not need to be kept at range: let it hit you a few times, below 15% the wand finishes it.",
    ["9e5f918"] = "Scorch fills the gaps even with the monster on you.",
    ["ab79a6b"] = "Open with Frostfire Bolt from afar, then one or two Arcane Blasts until Missile Barrage triggers and the missiles. Fire Blast on cooldown, Scorch to fill the gaps, the wand for the last 15%.",
    ["bece8ec"] = "Pyroblast and Heating Up: every non-periodic crit of Fireball, Frostfire Bolt, Fire Blast or Scorch makes your next Pyroblast a quarter faster, up to 3 charges, and Fire Blast adds a charge with every damage. Cast Pyroblast when Heating Up reaches 3 charges.",
    ["196edb9"] = "For every spec spell power comes first. Intellect raises mana and a little crit; Spirit reduces the pauses to drink.",
    ["38bc29a"] = "Frost starts with Precision: two points bring the chance to hit monsters of your level to 100%.",
    ["c690916"] = "Frostbite: your chilling effects have a 15% chance to freeze the target for 5 seconds. Ice Lance (from 27): against a frozen target it does 300% more, with an 8 second cooldown shared with Fire Blast.",
    ["1f1ed9a"] = "Frostbolt from afar, and keep casting while the monster arrives. When Frostbite freezes the target: a Frostbolt with Ice Lance right behind it; if Ice Lance is not ready, Cone of Cold. In melee: Frost Nova and step back, then Frostbolt and Ice Lance on the frozen monster. Missile Barrage: cast the missiles, or keep it for the next monster if this one is almost dead. Fire Blast or the wand for a low monster that is not frozen.",
    ["2e43c7c"] = "With Fingers of Frost your next two spells treat the target as frozen: the first on a Frostbolt, the second on a Frostbolt with Ice Lance (or with Cone of Cold if Ice Lance is not ready yet). Its strength is in the 30s: after Shatter a frozen target takes your hardest hits.",
    ["cecd125"] = "Ice Barrier first, and cast it again when the minute runs out: besides the shield it gives 15% more frost damage for a minute.",
    ["959453a"] = "Winter's Chill: Frostbolt and Ice Lance stack it on the target up to 5 times, and the next Cone of Cold does 20% more for each charge.",
    ["5a9d3eb"] = "Redemption (class quest)",
    ["3d343ad"] = "Seal of Command (Retribution talent), Seal of Justice",
    ["32b558d"] = "Dual specialization and mount",
    ["38d0905"] = "Before the pull Blessing of Might and Devotion Aura. Then three steps: Seal of Righteousness, Judgment while you run toward the monster, Holy Strike. After that, Judgment and Holy Strike every time they are ready, and refresh the seal only when it is about to end (Judgment no longer consumes it and is off the global cooldown). Mana is also your healing: if the next hit kills the monster, skip the button. If you finish a fight with mana left over turn it into health with Holy Light. In danger: first Divine Protection on yourself, then heal.",
    ["f580de7"] = "Consecration when you fight several enemies or have extra mana: it costs more than Judgment and Holy Strike together and needs 8 seconds to do all its damage. Exorcism on every undead or demon, even from 30 yards.",
    ["2ea2c89"] = "Add Hammer of Wrath: it finishes enemies under 20% health.",
    ["c8d4778"] = "Retribution and Protection start in the same tree with almost the same talents. In place of Deflection (5% parry) you can choose Benediction: all instant abilities cost 10% less mana, and Consecration becomes easier to afford.",
    ["a81d5b1"] = "With Seal of Command: Blessing of Kings or Might and Retribution Aura. On a monster that lasts: first Judgment of Seal of the Crusader (the monster takes more holy damage), then switch to Seal of Command if you have a slow weapon; with a fast weapon or lots of spell damage Seal of Righteousness is better. Then Judgment and Holy Strike on every cooldown. Trick: the Judgment of Seal of Command does almost double against a stunned target, so open with Hammer of Justice and then Judgment.",
    ["733e5e6"] = "Sacred Arbiter: Holy Strike hits 20% harder and refreshes every Judgment on the target, even those of other paladins.",
    ["a01f90a"] = "Champion of the Light turns up to 60% of your Intellect into spell damage: gear with spell power becomes even better. At 40 Unsealed Wrath: hits keep a copy of the active seal (up to 3), and switching seals is worth it again.",
    ["5f3698b"] = "The weapon is the most important thing: ideally with spell power and lots of damage. With Seal of Command slow, heavy weapons are the best (Holy Strike and the seal do more damage). On the rest first Strength or attack power, then Stamina, then spell power.",
    ["a531e3f"] = "Seal of Fury is the tank's seal: every hit does extra holy damage and with a shield you get an absorb equal to half of that damage. Its Judgment makes you taunt for 3 seconds from 10 yards. Righteous Fury raises all your threat by 33%. From 22 you move into the Protection tree, after Pursuit of Justice.",
    ["8279baa"] = "Blessing of Kings, Retribution Aura and Righteous Fury active. Always keep Seal of Fury up. Judge while you run toward the monster to taunt. Put down Consecration as soon as you are in melee, if mana allows. Then Holy Strike on every cooldown and Exorcism on undead and demons. Gather up to four enemies and burn everything with Consecration.",
    ["34e2900"] = "Shield Specialization: a block gives you back 4% of your maximum mana, at most every 3 seconds: it is a large part of your mana.",
    ["cc3ac76"] = "Templar's Bulwark: a shield that absorbs damage equal to all your health for 8 seconds, but gives you Forbearance for a minute. From 37 Swift Judgement: the seal's Judgment fires by itself with a 1 minute cooldown, so you have a second taunt.",
    ["be55413"] = "Holy Shield: for 10 seconds you block more often and up to 4 blocks do holy damage. Reckoning (from 43) can give an extra attack after a block or a critical hit taken.",
    ["e76d8e9"] = "For Protection spell power comes first (Seal of Fury, Holy Shield and Consecration do holy damage), then Strength and Stamina. For the weapon a faster one is better: Seal of Fury strikes on every hit. A weapon with spell power can be worth a bit less damage.",
    ["05e5db7"] = "Shadow Word: Pain; short class quest (a robe)",
    ["c95888a"] = "Mind Blast, Resurrection; the race quest teaches the first ability only of your race",
    ["091c0cd"] = "Holy Fire, Flash Heal, Devouring Plague, Fear Ward, Mind Soothe, Shackle Undead; the second racial ability",
    ["71b2a72"] = "Fortitude on yourself before the pull. Open with Smite, put Shadow Word: Pain on the target and finish it with the wand, which costs no mana and at the start does a large part of your damage (stand still half a second before using it). If the monster reaches you, Power Word: Shield first. The most important thing to have is a good wand: replace it every time you find a better one.",
    ["e023128"] = "Mind Blast is the strong hit with a short cooldown. The first seven talent points are the same for all specs: Wand Specialization (10-11) and Spirit Tap (12-16). With Spirit Tap, every kill of a monster that gives experience doubles your Spirit for 15 seconds and for that time half of your mana regeneration continues while you cast: fewer pauses to drink.",
    ["8df287d"] = "Inner Fire: extra armor, every hit you take uses a charge. Keep it, together with Fortitude, always on yourself and cast it again when it ends.",
    ["bebe913"] = "Psychic Scream makes nearby enemies run away, but beware: they can bring other monsters back.",
    ["ffa87bf"] = "The trainer teaches you more today than at any other level: Holy Fire (a slow but strong opener, it also burns over time), Flash Heal (fast but expensive), Devouring Plague (damage over time that heals you) and others.",
    ["084f80e"] = "Shadow is the recommended spec for leveling alone: the points go into Shadow Word: Pain, Mind Blast and Mind Flay, so monsters die sooner.",
    ["f33a503"] = "Put Shield on yourself if the monster reaches you. Open with Mind Blast, then Shadow Word: Pain. From 27 also Devouring Plague and Mind Flay, and after Shadow Word: Pain add Vampiric Embrace so your shadow damage heals you. Then finish with the wand. If mana is low skip Devouring Plague and Mind Flay.",
    ["496ef3d"] = "Shadow Word: Death is sudden damage, but if the target survives you take 30% of your maximum health: keep it for the final blow.",
    ["edd0d02"] = "Shadowform: stay in Shadowform while you fight (+10% shadow damage, shadow spells cost half the mana, -15% physical damage, but you cannot cast heals: leave it before healing). Open with Mind Blast, then Shadow Word: Pain, Vampiric Embrace, Devouring Plague and Mind Flay. When one more hit kills the monster: Shadow Word: Death, or leave the last bit to the wand. Shield on yourself if the monster reaches you.",
    ["b912dce"] = "For Shadow spell power comes first (shadow power is fine too: almost all your damage is shadow), then crit and Hit. The wand is very important: at the start it does a large part of the damage.",
    ["8e3f775"] = "Discipline is the healing spec we recommend for playing alone: from 20 Power in Light adds damage to Smite.",
    ["916c9c2"] = "Open with Holy Fire from afar, Smite while the monster arrives, then Mind Blast, Shadow Word: Pain and the wand. If the fight goes badly: Shield on yourself, then heal: Flash Heal if you need it fast, Heal if you have time.",
    ["a80f7e5"] = "Penance: a burst of holy hits that hurts an enemy or heals an ally, 12 second cooldown, the first hit lands at once.",
    ["037a666"] = "First Shield on yourself. Open with Holy Fire from afar. Smite while the monster walks, then Penance on the same target because Power in Light makes it hit harder. Then Mind Blast and Shadow Word: Pain. To finish Shadow Word: Death if one hit kills, otherwise the wand. Every time Weakened Soul disappears you can protect yourself again.",
    ["9d0affc"] = "Power Infusion: +20% damage and healing for 15 seconds, on yourself or a friend: cast it on yourself right before opening, every time it is ready. At 60 Inner Focus for emergencies: the next spell is free.",
    ["8e7cd8d"] = "For Discipline and Holy look for healing power and mana regeneration, then Intellect and Spirit. Choose the weapon with these same stats: it does not matter whether it is a staff or a one-hander with an off hand.",
    ["c5c1351"] = "Put Shield and Renew on yourself before the pull. Then open with Holy Fire, Smite while the monster arrives, Mind Blast and Shadow Word: Pain. Finish with Shadow Word: Death if it kills or with the wand.",
    ["575bdd0"] = "Holy Nova damages every nearby enemy and heals the group: it costs a lot of mana, so use it with several enemies on you, or when it is free (Searing Light from 43: Holy Fire can make the next Holy Nova free).",
    ["6953353"] = "Before the pull put Shield, Renew and Prayer of Mending on yourself (it heals the next time the target takes damage and then jumps to another in the group, 10 second cooldown).",
    ["a5c9096"] = "For Holy look for healing power and mana regeneration, then Intellect and Spirit. Choose the weapon with these same stats.",
    ["aa71e89"] = "Backstab (needs a dagger, only from behind), Pick Pocket",
    ["2e3c463"] = "Slice and Dice, Sprint, Sap; class quest (Blade of Cunning)",
    ["3a2246d"] = "Ambush (needs a dagger), Poised (passive)",
    ["8abd601"] = "Rupture; poison quest: Instant Poison and Crippling Poison",
    ["6c840ea"] = "Shank (new in Forever)",
    ["f3d428e"] = "Mutilate (Assassination talent)",
    ["3e307c7"] = "Death Mark (Subtlety talent), Slice and Dice rank 2",
    ["f14c847"] = "Shank rank 2",
    ["a554ba3"] = "Walk up to the monster and use Sinister Strike while you have combo points, then Eviscerate: more points, stronger hit. Stealth can stay on the bar for now. If the fight goes badly: Evasion and Gouge to stop a cast or gain a few seconds.",
    ["44b2b7e"] = "Slice and Dice (a finisher: you attack 20% faster, longer with more points), Sprint (50% faster for 15 seconds, does not break Stealth) and Sap to take a humanoid out of the fight before starting.",
    ["665b56f"] = "Rupture: a longer bleed with more points. With the poison quest, Instant Poison and Crippling Poison.",
    ["d06b2e0"] = "Shank: an off hand hit that cannot miss; the first rank costs 5 energy, gives back 15 and recharges in 10 seconds. From 26 Cheap Shot from stealth: it stuns for 4 seconds and gives 2 points.",
    ["6974c7f"] = "Combat is the duelist: it fights in melee with the weapon you prefer, works with any weapon and does not need stealth to begin. It is the one recommended for leveling alone.",
    ["cea5a19"] = "Riposte: after a parry of yours it lights up and hits for one and a half times the weapon's damage, disarms the monster for 6 seconds and costs only 10 energy with a 6 second cooldown.",
    ["5288c4d"] = "Instant Poison on both weapons. Cheap Shot from stealth for a hard fight, otherwise Sinister Strike right away. Riposte right after a parry. Sinister Strike for the points with Shank on cooldown: the first five points into Slice and Dice, the next five into Eviscerate.",
    ["869d1bf"] = "With two monsters on you: Blade Flurry (every 2 minutes, for 15 seconds you attack 20% faster and every hit also strikes a second nearby one).",
    ["9fb5eb8"] = "Adrenaline Rush (every 5 minutes: energy comes back twice as fast for 15 seconds) for a dangerous monster.",
    ["f8cc28b"] = "Cold Blood right before a big Eviscerate.",
    ["625324b"] = "Leather armor with Agility: it is the one you want. Hit, crit, attack power and Stamina are useful. Combat can use any type of weapon, because Hack and Slash gives a bonus for each: swords and axes, daggers and fist weapons, maces.",
    ["d01cb25"] = "Assassination is the poisoner: poisons and finishers get stronger and stronger, and at 40 Mutilate arrives.",
    ["9eb3d72"] = "Instant Poison on both weapons. From stealth open with Garrote or Cheap Shot. Sinister Strike for the points and Shank on cooldown. Slice and Dice, then Eviscerate; keep Cold Blood for a big Eviscerate.",
    ["33aceb3"] = "Venom: for 6 seconds after every Shank your poisons hit 30% harder and 20% more often. Shank on cooldown.",
    ["88ede56"] = "Mutilate builds the points: it hits with both weapons, 20% harder on a poisoned target, and gives 2 points. You need two daggers. Slice and Dice, Shank on cooldown for Venom, then Eviscerate; Cold Blood on a big Eviscerate.",
    ["20500ff"] = "Leather armor with Agility. Assassination needs daggers for Backstab, Ambush and Mutilate. Hit, crit, attack power and Stamina are useful.",
    ["5259278"] = "Subtlety is the ambusher: it opens every fight from the shadows with a dagger in hand.",
    ["64f4a07"] = "Dagger in the main hand, Instant Poison on both weapons. Get behind the monster, Premeditation, then Ambush, then Ghostly Strike, then Garrote. Sinister Strike builds the rest; Shank on cooldown for energy; Eviscerate finishes.",
    ["37c1365"] = "Hemorrhage builds the points in place of Sinister Strike.",
    ["c0f22d5"] = "Hemorrhage and Shank build the points, and with Boot Knife every Shank is worth two. Death Mark stores damage for 6 seconds: spend a full set of points on it when the monster lives long enough, then Eviscerate to finish. If the fight goes badly, Preparation resets Premeditation, Ghostly Strike and your other cooldowns.",
    ["a993dd2"] = "Leather armor with Agility. Subtlety keeps a dagger in the main hand (Ambush and Backstab require it). Hit, crit, attack power and Stamina are useful.",
    ["abbb551"] = "Earth Shock; earth totem quest: Stoneskin Totem",
    ["8e8845b"] = "Fire totem quest: Searing Totem",
    ["2be8a5e"] = "Ghost Wolf, Frost Shock, Lesser Healing Wave, Frostbrand Weapon, Healing Stream Totem (water totem quest), Call of the Elements, Totemic Recall",
    ["0a8c77d"] = "Windfury Weapon, Reincarnation (needs an Ankh), Astral Recall, Grounding Totem",
    ["47fd721"] = "Chain Lightning, Windfury Totem; air totem quest (the storm weapons)",
    ["b821239"] = "Chain Heal, mail armor",
    ["d6b5209"] = "Rockbiter Weapon stays on the weapon and from 8 Lightning Shield goes up before the pull. Open with Lightning Bolt and as soon as it arrives Earth Shock, which is instant; against a caster keep the shock to interrupt its cast. When the monster is on you the melee hits finish it. If another monster arrives put down Earthbind Totem: it slows it and lets you kite. After the fight Healing Wave if you are hurt.",
    ["fa734a3"] = "Every spec has a clear role: Enhancement fights in melee with a big weapon, totems and shocks; Elemental stays at range with Lightning Bolt, Chain Lightning and Fire Nova; Restoration heals and stays in a group or in dungeons, not alone doing quests. If you run out of mana Enhancement keeps hitting (the kill takes longer), Elemental suffers more.",
    ["b74be3c"] = "Flame Shock hits at once with fire and then burns for 12 seconds. Flametongue Weapon adds fire damage to every hit; Searing Totem is a small turret that shoots a nearby enemy.",
    ["35c7293"] = "Enhancement is the spec we recommend for quests. It has its weak points: a poor weapon lowers the damage a lot, the mana costs at the start weigh heavily and against many enemies at once it struggles.",
    ["028a6b7"] = "Stormstrike hits at once with the weapon's full damage every 8 seconds, and the target takes 20% more from your next Lightning Bolt, Chain Lightning or Earth Shock.",
    ["a94041d"] = "Stormstrike every time it is ready, and right after it Earth Shock (the Stormstrike hit makes the shock stronger). Rockbiter Weapon always on the weapon and Lightning Shield on yourself. Before the pull Strength of Earth and Mana Spring and, if mana allows, Searing Totem or Magma Totem. Open with Lightning Bolt rank 1 (the cheapest), then the normal hits do the rest. Fire Nova only if the monsters are in the range of your fire totem and you still have mana. After the kill Healing Wave, and drink if mana is low.",
    ["18a8896"] = "Windfury Weapon on the weapon in place of Rockbiter: every hit has a 20% chance to give two extra attacks, it is the big piece of Enhancement. If a dodge or parry resets Stormstrike, press it again at once. Windfury Totem, with Grounding Totem in its place against casters.",
    ["f3777c4"] = "Maelstrom Weapon: your hits build up to 5 charges and every charge makes the next Lightning Bolt faster and cheaper: at 5 charges cast Lightning Bolt at the highest rank. From 46 Water Shield takes the place of Lightning Shield (you can only have one).",
    ["022a55d"] = "For Enhancement the weapon matters above all: the ideal is a slow two-hander, between 3.3 and 3.8 speed. Then Strength and attack power, with Intellect right behind, because it feeds Mental Dexterity and mana.",
    ["4540d89"] = "Earthbound: when you put down Earthbind Totem nearby enemies stay stuck for 5 seconds.",
    ["bcd1d77"] = "Before the pull Mana Spring Totem and a fire totem (Searing against one monster, Magma against several), Lightning Shield on yourself. Open at the edge of range with Lightning Bolt, put Flame Shock on the target and keep going with Lightning Bolt. With three or more monsters Fire Nova every time it is ready. Earth Shock interrupts a caster and brings it to you. Earthbind Totem when monsters get close. Heal and drink at the end.",
    ["13a3832"] = "Against a single monster: Searing Totem, open from afar with Lightning Bolt, Flame Shock, keep going with Lightning Bolt. Against three or more: Magma Totem, open with Chain Lightning, Flame Shock on one of them, then Chain Lightning and Fire Nova on every cooldown with Lightning Bolt in between.",
    ["2c3ba7a"] = "Lightning Mastery (15 seconds, then 3 minutes): for 15 seconds Lightning Bolt casts faster and Chain Lightning ignores its cooldown. Use it on an elite or a big pull, otherwise on every cooldown.",
    ["b56c9ed"] = "Water Shield takes the place of Lightning Shield on yourself.",
    ["4688073"] = "For Elemental look for spell power, with Intellect mainly for mana. From level 40 you can wear mail.",
    ["b4ca62b"] = "Before the pull Water Shield, Mana Spring Totem and the totems the group can use. While someone takes damage, Healing Wave is the workhorse. Lesser Healing Wave casts in 1.5 seconds and heals less for the mana: keep it for the moments when time matters. Mana Tide Totem (12 seconds, 5 minute cooldown) when the whole group is out of mana. When nobody is in danger add damage: Lightning Bolt on a target, Fire Nova on a group. Drink at the end.",
    ["42937c0"] = "Nature's Swiftness (every 3 minutes): your next nature spell is instant, so an instant Healing Wave for a friend who is about to die. Windfury Totem if there are players in melee.",
    ["9b2d19c"] = "Riptide: healing over time with a 12 second cooldown, and a Chain Heal cast right on the target of Riptide is 25% stronger. Chain Heal heals the target and two other allies, so it covers damage spread across the group.",
    ["a86408d"] = "For Restoration look for healing power, with Intellect mainly for mana. From level 40 you can wear mail.",
    ["c86a1be"] = "Voidwalker (class quest), Drain Soul, Healthstone",
    ["40cb6b4"] = "Succubus and Incubus (class quests), Demon Armor, Curse of the Elements, Rain of Fire, Ritual of Summoning",
    ["df7bfa2"] = "Felhunter (class quest), Hellfire",
    ["19e5308"] = "Howl of Terror, Felsteed (quest)",
    ["1c5b068"] = "The demon goes in first, then Bane of Agony and Corruption; only the toughest monsters get Immolate, because the demon holds them. The order matters because damage draws attention: the first ticks of Agony are small, so the demon holds the monster until a fresh Immolate hits hard enough to turn it toward you. Keep Demon Skin up, skip the DOTs on an almost dead monster and do not renew Agony while it is still doing damage. Until you have a wand Shadow Bolt finishes the job; then get a wand: every shot is mana saved for the next pull.",
    ["ea42414"] = "Drain Soul is your main source of Soul Shards: a non-trivial monster that dies from its drain always gives one. When you have few, finish your kills with it. Healthstone, Soul Stone and the summons of Voidwalker, Succubus and Felhunter require shards.",
    ["72f97d5"] = "Drain Life changes how you read the screen: if the blue bar is low and your health is fine, Life Tap; if your health has really dropped, Drain Life on the monster. This way almost all the downtime disappears.",
    ["51205f3"] = "Demon Armor in place of Demon Skin. With Ritual of Summoning you and two companions bring a group member who is still far away. A Fear gives you a few free seconds for a bandage.",
    ["9d83c05"] = "If you play alone, Affliction is the choice: accuracy and an instant Corruption arrive early. Curse of the Elements goes next to Agony. From 25 Nightfall can trigger from the damage of Corruption, Drain Life or Drain Soul, and the Shadow Bolt after the proc has no cast time. You can take the drain talent a little before 30 and lean on Drain Life in every fight.",
    ["04f03c2"] = "Siphon Life: a tick every 3 seconds for 30 seconds, so a monster that dies in 10 only gets a third of it. Keep it for long fights.",
    ["703c37f"] = "Demonic Sacrifice: you sacrifice the Felhunter and for two hours you recover 3% of your total health every 4 seconds; summoning a demon cancels it, so from here on you do quests almost without a pet.",
    ["2dbcea6"] = "Wrack: you channel for 6 seconds, it does shadow damage, and your other shadow DOTs on that target hit 10% harder while it lasts.",
    ["edb7e47"] = "Choose weapons with spell power, because you will almost never use them to hit. At the start a wand upgrade beats almost all others; later, spell power comes first. Stamina is extra health to turn into mana with Life Tap, Intellect a bigger mana pool, Spirit gives more with every Life Tap.",
    ["1c3a6a3"] = "If you prefer to watch the demon work, Demonology: with Demonic Brand from 25. From 25 Searing Pain puts a mark on the target for 10 seconds, and at most the first six hits of your demon do extra damage: renew it with a quick Searing Pain on what the demon is fighting and fill the gaps with DOTs and the wand.",
    ["00d4a86"] = "Soul Link: 30% of every direct hit on you goes to the demon, and the two of you do 3% more damage. It is lost when you change demon: cast it again every time.",
    ["a3cee7a"] = "Demonic Pact: the sacrifice survives a change of demon, unless you summon exactly the one you sacrificed. In a dungeon sacrifice the Imp (15% more shadow damage); on solo quests the Felhunter for its heals, and fight next to a Voidwalker, Succubus or Incubus. From 27 you can also level as Affliction and switch spec: you have the points for all three ranks of Demonic Brand.",
    ["545f2c9"] = "Destruction is playable from 10, but it becomes much stronger at 39 and 40, and it spends more time standing still casting than the other two: you can also choose it later.",
    ["0b5d29c"] = "Shadowburn: an instant hit that costs a Shard and gives it back if a non-trivial target dies within 8 seconds.",
    ["124afde"] = "The opening changes: Shadow Bolt from maximum range and Immolate while the bolt is still in flight. This way the monster comes to you and not to the demon, so choose fights you can end quickly. Shadowburn finishes monsters; it is better to keep Conflagrate for the end of your Immolate.",
    ["07ea333"] = "With Shadow and Flame, Conflagrate raises your shadow damage by 20% and Shadowburn your fire damage by 20%; Conflagrate no longer consumes Immolate and Shadowburn always gives the Shard back. From 39 there is no reason to hold them back.",
    ["609f38c"] = "Incinerate does 25% more to everything already burning from your Immolate.",
    ["a1d5005"] = "Defensive Stance, Taunt, Sunder Armor (class quest), Bloodrage",
    ["b87bfb2"] = "Revenge, Demoralizing Shout, Tactical Mastery (learned from the trainer)",
    ["a61955b"] = "Victory Rush, Cleave, Slam, Retaliation; you can use two weapons",
    ["323f468"] = "Berserker Stance, Berserker Rage, Intercept (class quest)",
    ["b289adb"] = "Plate armor and mount",
    ["2debde0"] = "Battle Shout before the pull, Charge, Rend on what lives long, then let the normal hits build rage. Heroic Strike only with rage you do not need: it replaces a normal hit and that hit gives no rage. With several monsters Thunder Clap; do not spend rage on a monster that is about to die.",
    ["f98c5d6"] = "Bloodrage between pulls: it costs a little health and gives 10 rage at once and 10 in 10 seconds. Never start a fight without rage.",
    ["970305a"] = "Victory Rush every time it lights up: after a kill that gives experience you have 20 seconds, it does damage and heals you for 10%, 30 second cooldown and costs no rage.",
    ["a60b4a3"] = "From 14 Revenge is your main attack: use it every time it lights up (after a block, a dodge or a parry). Switch to shield and a one-hand weapon. Thunder Clap and Demoralizing Shout on groups.",
    ["41fd2f0"] = "Charge, then stay in Defensive Stance. Keep Shield Block against anything that hits you in melee, and skip Shield Block against casters. Revenge every time it lights up; Rend and a few Sunder Armors on monsters that live long; Thunder Clap and Demoralizing Shout on groups.",
    ["b604238"] = "With Vanguard you can Charge from Defensive Stance: you can open a pull without changing stance, if you are out of combat.",
    ["c9e7c22"] = "Shield Wall: 60% less damage for 12 seconds, for pulls that go badly.",
    ["3f0c2f4"] = "Shield Slam is the strongest hit (the damage grows with your block value): use it first and Revenge right after. If you have little rage Revenge first, it costs less.",
    ["846367b"] = "Protection mainly wants Strength (every point gives 2 attack power and block value). For the weapon take the best DPS: Revenge and Shield Slam do not depend on the weapon. Agility matters less: it gives crit, dodge and armor but no attack power.",
    ["fabdcb6"] = "Rend first, then Overpower every time it lights up (after a dodge by the target).",
    ["f29cf52"] = "Rend, then Overpower when it lights up. From 20 Slam right after a hit.",
    ["60998aa"] = "Sweeping Strikes: your next five hits also strike a second nearby enemy, it is a big jump. Start on one monster while you have extra rage, then pull a second monster and use Sweeping Strikes and Cleave on both.",
    ["efc030d"] = "With Bloodthrill, if Rend is on the target your main hand hits have a 20% chance to trigger Overpower: Rend stays in the rotation until 60.",
    ["98a8fec"] = "Mortal Strike is your new main attack.",
    ["7caf705"] = "The weapon matters more than anything: look for the highest DPS, and for Arms a slow two-hander (every hit and Mortal Strike and Slam do more damage). On the rest first Hit (because a missed hit gives neither damage nor rage), then Strength and Crit. Agility gives crit and dodge but no attack power.",
    ["ce62f29"] = "Rend on monsters that live long, Overpower when the target dodges. If a second monster is next to the target, spend the extra rage on Cleave. Choose a fast off hand: more hits, more rage.",
    ["1879df1"] = "Death Wish: for 30 seconds you do 20% more physical damage and cannot be feared, but you take 5% more damage. Reckless Swings (31): it costs a little health and your next four hits give 5 more rage each.",
    ["0d27ce4"] = "With Whirlwind (level 36) it is your main button, even against a single monster: the cooldown drops to 8 seconds and it hits the nearest one for 30% more damage.",
    ["308a3c5"] = "Bloodthirst every time Whirlwind is on cooldown. From 50 you have Recklessness.",
    ["2d76abd"] = "The weapon matters more than anything: look for the highest DPS. For the off hand a fast one (more hits, more rage). On the rest first Hit, then Strength and Crit. Agility gives crit and dodge but no attack power.",
}
